# Rosin and the moon rock — the two items the extraction bench makes.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw these; that is what the .mctex is for.
#
# ## The family rule these have to obey
#
# Five concentrates now, and **the silhouette is what tells them apart**, never the shade. Colour in
# this trade records how resin was made and cured and does not predict potency at all, so a family
# that graded weak-to-strong by colour would be lying five times over.
#
#   item/hashish            an oblique slab      pressed in a mould     brown
#   item/charas             an irregular ball    hand-rolled            near-black
#   item/filtered_hashish   a loose heap         never pressed          blonde
#   item/rosin              a viscous glob       squeezed out hot       amber, and GLOSSY
#   item/moon_rock          a lumpy nug          coated, not made       green under a dark crust
#
# Rosin is the only one of the five that was ever a liquid, and that is its whole silhouette: a
# soft-edged pool with a pulled tail and a hard specular highlight. Every other member is matte.
# Items are high contrast (vanilla items span a median 164 luminance steps against a block's 76),
# which is what lets a 16x16 glob read as wet.

@palette default
. = none
1 = 3A2306      the shadow the glob casts, and its darkest rim
2 = 5C3A0B
3 = 7E520F
4 = A06D14      body
5 = C68A1C      the lit face
6 = E4AC34      near the highlight
7 = F6D06A      the wet sheen
8 = FFF0BC      the specular hit; ONE cluster, up-left, and nowhere else

# A pulled glob of rosin: wide and low, with a tail dragged up to the right the way a viscous
# extract lifts off a parchment. The tail is what stops this reading as a lump of amber.
@texture item/rosin 16x16 type=item
................
...........122..
..........12442.
.........124531.
........1245431.
...12211245431..
..1246788654321.
.12456788765432.
.12456776654431.
.124556655443321
.12344555443321.
.1233444433221..
..122333322211..
...1122222111...
.....111111.....
................

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The moon rock: two layers, exactly as a packed device is.
#
# Layer 0 is the crust -- hashish and rosin, the same on every strain, and untinted. Layer 1 is the
# bud showing through it, drawn as flat mid-grey and tinted at render time by StrainTintSource, so
# one texture covers Purple Kush, Lemon Haze and whatever comes third.
#
# That split is the whole reason this is one item instead of one per strain. It also means layer 1
# must be a single flat value: a shaded layer multiplied by a tint comes out muddy, and every tinted
# layer in this mod (the spliff's load, each device's load) is flat for the same reason.
@palette crust extends=default
. = none
a = 15100B      the deepest crevice in the crust
b = 241B12
c = 342718
d = 46331F      body of the crust
e = 5C4429
f = 786134      a granule catching the light
g = 9A8248      the sparkle a kief coat actually has; scattered, never a band

@texture item/moon_rock 16x16 type=item palette=crust
................
................
.....bccba......
...abdefedcb....
..abdefgfedcb...
.abdefggfedccb..
.acefgggfedccbb.
abdefggfedcbbba.
abdeffedccbbbaa.
abcdeedccbbbaaa.
.abcdedccbbaaa..
.abccddccbbaa...
..abcccbbaaa....
...abbbaaa......
................
................

# The bud, seen through the gaps in the crust. Flat by necessity (see above) and deliberately
# sparse -- a moon rock is mostly crust, and green showing everywhere would make it look like a bud
# with a shadow rather than a nug that has been dipped in something.
@palette load
. = none
G = 8F8F8F      flat mid-grey; StrainTintSource multiplies the strain's own colour into it
@texture item/moon_rock_load 16x16 type=item palette=load
................
................
................
....GG..........
....GG...GG.....
.........GG.....
..GG........GG..
..GG..GG....GG..
......GG........
....GG......GG..
....GG......GG..
..........GG....
..........GG....
................
................
................

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two loose intermediates the Sifting Box makes.
#
# NEITHER IS PRESSED, and the silhouette has to say so or the family collapses into "hash in five
# shades". Both are LOOSE HEAPS with broken, granular top edges -- the shape of powder tipped out of
# a screen -- against the slab of item/hashish, the ball of item/charas and the glob of item/rosin.
#
# They differ from each other only in tone, and that is correct: kief and bubble hash are the same
# trichome heads separated two ways. What ice-water buys is that there is almost no leaf in it, so
# the washed one is paler and less muddy -- and NOT brighter or more saturated, because a colour
# that read as "stronger" would be the one lie this whole family refuses to tell.

@palette kief
. = none
1 = 4A3418      the shadow under the heap, and its rim
2 = 6B4E24
3 = 8A6A33
4 = A98844      the body
5 = C2A055      lit face
6 = DCBC7B      grains catching the light
7 = F0D9A6      the brightest grains; scattered, never a band

@texture item/kief 16x16 type=item palette=kief
................
................
................
.......56.......
......4671......
....234677532...
...12456776431..
..1245677654321.
.124456665443211
.123445554433211
.122334444332211
..1223333322211.
...112222221111.
.....11111111...
................
................

# The washed one: the same heap, a shade paler and cooler, with the leaf-brown taken out of the
# shadows. Read side by side they are obviously the same substance, which is the point.
@palette bubble extends=kief
1 = 5A5240      damp shadow -- greyer than kief's, because there is no leaf left in it to be brown
2 = 7A7157
3 = 9A9070
4 = B8AC88      the body
5 = CFC29C
6 = E4D8B6      grains catching the light
7 = F6EFD6      the brightest grains

@texture item/bubble_hash 16x16 type=item from=item/kief palette=bubble

# Kief put over the screen a second time. Same heap, same grain, one shade blonder and cleaner --
# less leaf through a finer mesh really is blonder, and that is ALL it is. It must not read as
# stronger, and it must not read as bubble hash either: the washed one is cool and grey-shadowed
# where this one stays warm, because a dry screen never takes the leaf-brown out of the shadows the
# way water does.
@palette filtered_kief extends=kief
1 = 5E4522      shadow -- still warm, unlike bubble hash's grey
2 = 82632F
3 = A5813F
4 = C29B52      the body
5 = D9B570
6 = ECD096
7 = FAE7BE      the brightest grains

@texture item/filtered_kief 16x16 type=item from=item/kief palette=filtered_kief
